      "message": "Nope, this isn\u0027t quite right (crashes one of my test devices). Looks like this assumes that the kernel\u0027s version of the address is somewhere else (identity-mapped with phys address).\n\nI could use flush_cache_range() instead which would be fine except that it\u0027s a non-standard, non-exported function (the very thing I\u0027m trying to get rid of which this CL).\n\nSo, I guess I need to use the \"right\" kernel address for patching... new attempt coming.",
