      "writtenOn": "2018-08-14T15:47:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "An mb() wouldn\u0027t suffice for a VIVT cache since the modification to pageX from vaA is not visible at vaB unless there is an explicit flush (and we can ensure that vaB is not stale in the cache). If there is physical tagging (as in x86, arm64 and the other modern architectures) then the flush isn\u0027t necessary since the modification at vaA will cause an invalidation of the cacheline for vaB so coherency is maintained across aliases.\n\nI have a patch that does the flush correctly by using the \"standard\" kernel VA (it adds some complexity though), but now I\u0027m concerned about Arve\u0027s statement that there might be a stale \"vaB\" -- the user space VA -- that needs to be flushed too. I don\u0027t understand why that would be needed given the full cache flush at the context switch for VIVT and no use of the vaB page here... Arve can you explain?",
      "parentUuid": "0c9d552d_9b1b6ea7",
      "revId": "5991bb5cec3cf9e6ab3ab4238ee58fe640f27b2c",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "aefa5ec9_be1d522c",
        "filename": "drivers/android/binder.c",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 4014,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000205
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-08-14T17:46:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "There won\u0027t be any stale data in vaB if you came here from a process context switch, but that is not necessarily how you get here. You could get here after the current thread calls the ioctl which means it could have pulled data into the cache, or you could get here from another thread. The CPUs that have VIVT caches don\u0027t typically fetch a lot of data speculatively, and have only one core, so the chances are low that the cache-line that has a fd in it would be fetched after the sender ran. If the fd is near the start or end of the buffer though it could share a cache-line with an active transaction and cause problems even with no speculation.",
      "parentUuid": "aca0358a_8ff95057",
      "revId": "5991bb5cec3cf9e6ab3ab4238ee58fe640f27b2c",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
